title: I Am: The Names of Christ in John
description: The seven “I am” figures, the five “I am he” sayings and “Before Abraham was, I am”: how Jesus declares Himself the I AM of Exodus 3:14 in the Gospel of John, and why believing that He is “I am” is life or death.
output: lessons/bible/john-i-am.html
highlight: I am

# Pulled out of "That Ye Might Believe" (john-that-ye-might-believe.deck) on Nov 18, 2026, at the author's request, to be fleshed out
# later as its own lesson. Slides are as they stood in that deck, in the same order.

=== Introduction
--- I Am [title]
overline: The Gospel of John
sub: The seven figures, the five “I am he” sayings and “Before Abraham was, I am”: Jesus declares Himself the I AM.
refs: Exodus 3:14; John 8:58

=== The Seven “I Am” Figures
--- The Seven “I Am” Figures
kicker: The figures
big: Exodus 3:14
lead: Jesus uses the misunderstanding motif to declare His divinity in a picture, and each carries the gospel inside it: **believe on Him.**
tile: [[John 6:35]] | The bread of life
tile: [[John 8:12]] | The light of the world
tile: [[John 10:9]] | The door
tile: [[John 10:11]] | The good shepherd
tile: [[John 11:25-26]] | The resurrection, and the life
tile: [[John 14:6]] | The way, the truth, and the life
tile: [[John 15:1]] | The true vine

--- 1. The Bread of Life
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 6:35
lit: The literal hearer | John 6:52
take: Coming is compared to eating; believing to drinking.

--- 2. The Light of the World
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 8:12
rev: Restated | John 12:46
lit: The literal hearer | John 9:40

--- 3. The Door
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 10:9
lit: The hearers | John 10:6
take: One way into the fold. They understood not, so He said it again a different way.

--- 4. The Good Shepherd
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 10:11
rev: The figure points to the cross | John 10:17-18

--- 5. The Resurrection, and the Life
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 11:25-26
lit: The literal hearer, Martha | John 11:24
take: Martha thought of the last day. Jesus pointed her to Himself, the Life standing before her.

--- 6. The Way, the Truth, and the Life
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 14:6
lit: The literal hearer, Thomas | John 14:5
take: Thomas thought of a road. The way is a Person.

--- 7. The True Vine
kicker: The seven “I am” figures
big: John 15:1
rev: Joined to Him | John 15:5
take: Life and fruit come only by being joined to Him.

=== The Five “I Am He” Sayings
--- The Five “I Am He” Sayings
kicker: The bare “I am”
tile: [[John 4:26]] | I that speak unto thee am *he*
tile: [[John 8:24]] | Ye shall die in your sins
tile: [[John 8:28]] | When ye have lifted up the Son of man
tile: [[John 13:19]] | That ye may believe that I am *he*
tile: [[John 18:5-6]] | I am *he*

--- 1. I That Speak unto Thee Am He
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 4
lit: The hearer | John 4:25
fig: His words | John 4:26
rev: The meaning | John 4:28-29
take: She looked for a Messiah someday. He was standing in front of her.

--- 2. Ye Shall Die in Your Sins
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 8
fig: His words | John 8:24
lit: The hearers, the Jews | John 8:25
rev: The meaning | John 8:27
take: They asked for a name; He had already given it. Believing that He is “I am” is life or death.

--- 3. When Ye Have Lifted Up the Son of Man
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 8
fig: His words | John 8:28
lit: The hearers | John 8:30
rev: The meaning | John 12:32-33
take: The cross would prove who He is.

--- 4. That Ye May Believe That I Am He
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 13
fig: The figure | John 13:18
rev: His words | John 13:19

--- 4. That Ye May Believe That I Am He, continued
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 13
lit: The hearers | John 13:22
lit: The hearers again | John 13:28
take: The disciples missed it at the table. Once the betrayal came to pass, the fulfilled word would prove He is “I am.”

--- 5. I Am He
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 18
fig: His question | John 18:4
lit: The hearers | John 18:5
lit: Their response | John 18:6

--- 5. I Am He, continued
kicker: The five “I am he” sayings · John 18
rev: The meaning | John 18:8-9
take: They came for a man from Nazareth. At the name of God they fell, and He gave Himself up to keep His own.

=== Before Abraham Was, I Am
--- Before Abraham Was, I Am
kicker: John 8
lead: The final declaratory “I AM” to the Pharisees. Abraham rejoiced to see His day ([[John 8:56]]); the Jews answered, “Thou art not yet fifty years old” ([[John 8:57]]).
big: John 8:58
lit: Their response | John 8:59
take: They counted His age in years. He spoke as the eternal God.

